  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "directions",
      "page": "page-0",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Three ways to answer the same question: a partner opens Home, and there is nothing on it.\n\nEach bets on a different axis — A on \"we are looking for you right now\", B on \"here is your day\", C on \"you are on\". The animations are live; give them a few seconds each.\n\nMotion & offline (far right) compares the three side by side and shows what offline has to look like."
    },
    {
      "id": "journey",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 820,
      "text": "Four tabs now: Home · Work · Money · Me.\n\nHome (1) is status — availability, today's money, three figures, and the radar while dispatch looks for work. It has two faces: idle, and with work in (1b). Nothing that needs the vendor is ever hidden behind a link.\n\nWork (2) is the full list, grouped by whose move it is. The Work menu item lands straight here.\n\nEvery frame is 360 wide — the mid-range Android this runs on."
    },
    {
      "id": "spec-note",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -130,
      "w": 620,
      "text": "Left: the three controls that render together on the job screen today, and what replaces them.\n\nRight: every measurement the screens are built from - grid, type ramp, icon scale, control tiers."
    }
  ],
